      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How do I stop my spouse selling our house during divorce?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Apply to the Court of Urgent Matters for a precautionary attachment (Hajz Ihtiyati) on the property. File ex-parte (without notifying your spouse) showing a financial claim exceeding AED 10,000 and risk of dissipation. If granted, the DLD registers the attachment against the title, blocking any transfer or sale. The order is issued within 48 hours in urgent cases. You must then file the substantive case within 8 days. Once the DLD registers the attachment, the property cannot be transferred at any Registration Trustee centre.',
